{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy utility tradeoff privacy utility tradeoff","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","fileName":"Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy-Utility Tradeoff","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 09:32\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Data Ethics and Digital Power]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"privacy utility tradeoff privacy utility tradeoff","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","fileName":"Privacy-Utility Tradeoff.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Privacy-Utility Tradeoff","heading":"Privacy-Utility Tradeoff","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Privacy-preserving analysis often reduces the detail available about an individual while retaining useful population-level evidence. In the book's randomized-response example, some survey answers are deliberately obscured by a secret coin flip, yet the proportion of true answers can be estimated across the group.\n\nMore noise can strengthen protection but reduce analytical precision. Differential-privacy methods formalize this tension for data collection and queries. Keeping source data on participating devices, as in federated learning, changes a different part of the tradeoff: raw records need not be centralized, although shared model updates still require privacy scrutiny.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Data Ethics and Digital Power","datascience_mit.epub"],"properties":[